{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory contains a serious preventable responsibility-chain insulin error: the doctor gave concrete remote correction-dose advice despite incomplete current insulin/diet context, and the family then reported following it with hypoglycemia-type symptoms. This mandates grade 1 even though the doctor later repeatedly addressed stroke/swallowing red flags, held old rheumatoid drugs, used records, and helped obtain an endocrinology bridging plan. Closure became more executable later, but the earlier serious RC2 commission cannot be erased by later mitigation.",
